; DOMAIN: local-shtuka [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: A mixed-characteristic local shtuka (Scholze-Weinstein) over a perfectoid affinoid S=Spa(R,R+) in char p is a G-bundle on the relative Fargues-Fontaine curve X_S (or on the punctured Spd of B_dR^+) together with a Frobenius-semilinear modification (meromorphic along a Cartier divisor of untilts / legs), i.e. an iso of the two Frobenius pullbacks away from the legs bounded by cocharacters mu. The moduli of local shtukas with one leg and bounded modification type mu = the local Shimura variety / Rapoport-Zink space at infinite level, a diamond over Spd E (E the reflex field); it carries commuting Hecke (geometric Satake, bounded by mu) and G(Q_p) x J_b(Q_p) actions realizing local Langlands. Scholze-Weinstein prove Rapoport-Zink spaces and their local models are represented by such shtuka moduli, unifying p-adic Hodge theory (the modification = a B_dR^+-lattice, i.e. a p-adic Hodge structure / de Rham datum) with the geometrization on Bun_G (a shtuka is a point of the Hecke stack Hck_G over Bun_G).
; Bridge: genesis_geometric_satake (the boundedness of the shtuka modification by a dominant cocharacter mu IS the Schubert/Satake datum on the B_dR^+-affine Grassmannian; Hecke operators bounded by mu act on shtuka moduli) + genesis_bun_g (a local shtuka is exactly a modification of G-bundles, i.e. a point of the Hecke correspondence Hck_G -> Bun_G x Bun_G; shtuka moduli map to Bun_G) + genesis_fargues_fontaine (shtukas live on the relative FF curve X_S with legs = untilt divisors, the modification meromorphic along those legs).
(= (local-shtuka $G $S) (modification (frobenius-pullback (G-bundle (relative-ff-curve $S))) (bounded-by (leg $S))))
(= (legs (local-shtuka $G $S)) (cartier-divisor (untilts $S)))
(= (boundedness (local-shtuka $G $S)) (schubert (dominant-cocharacter $mu)))
(= (shtuka-moduli $G $mu) (diamond (local-shimura-variety $G $mu) (spd (reflex-field $mu))))
(= (rapoport-zink $G $b $mu) (infinite-level (shtuka-moduli $G $mu)))
(= (symmetries (shtuka-moduli $G $mu)) (product (hecke (geometric-satake $G)) (times ($G (Q-p)) ($J-b (Q-p)))))
(= (shtuka-to-bun-G $s) (point (hecke-correspondence (bun-G $G))))